    "notes": "Polylactic Acid (PLA) printed via FDM. Bio-derived and compostable under industrial conditions. Stiffest common FDM material but brittle — low elongation to failure with no clear yield point. Very low max service temperature (52 °C per Simplify3D) limits use in any warm environment (car interiors, outdoor direct sun). Properties are anisotropic; inter-layer (Z) strength significantly lower than XY. Not recommended for structural parts in humid or UV-exposed environments."
